# .vercelignore — files/directories EXCLUDED from the serverless bundle.
# .vercelignore lists EXCLUSIONS only: everything not listed below is
# included, which keeps the import-traced domain graph (runtime/, backends/,
# contracts/, developerapi/, agent/, protocol/, evidence/, executionplans/,
# adapters/, offers/, capabilities/, policy/, eligibility/, assurance/,
# replan/, resilience/) in the deployment. Rationale: a smaller, faster
# bundle with no governance/CI/operator files shipped to production.
# (.git/ and __pycache__/ artifacts are excluded automatically by Vercel.)
#
# spec/schemas/ is RUNTIME DATA, not governance: the accepted domain
# authorities machine-load spec/schemas/protocol.json (protocol/
# versioning.py) and the registries under spec/schemas/registries/
# (capabilities/, adapters/validation.py, identity/profiles.py) at request
# time — the first production deployment's live acceptance proved the
# exclusion of spec/ wholesale starves the demonstration path (the typed
# "missing access-profile registry" failure). spec/'s OTHER children stay
# excluded: the architect package, the ACR/registries, the frozen
# architecture documents, and the historical/research material are
# governance, never runtime.
spec/acr/
spec/architect/
spec/experience/
spec/history/
spec/integration/
spec/migration/
spec/prompts/
spec/research/
spec/application-model.md
spec/architecture-1.1-proposed.md
spec/architecture-lock-1.1-proposed.md
spec/architecture-lock.md
spec/architecture.md
spec/change-control.md
spec/dependency-graph-1.1.md
spec/dependency-graph.md
spec/governance.md
spec/mission.md
spec/work-items-1.1.md
spec/work-items.md
spec/workflow.md

# the operator/CI surface (never production)
tools/
.github/
deploy/
worker-charters/
docs/

# root-level markdown (README/AGENTS/etc.) — none of it is needed at runtime
/*.md
